div.p:
@field isn't an xqDoc tag: the extension adds it, in the same style, for documenting
				records. A field name that isn't an NCName is quoted, as in the record type - for example
				@field 'unit name' e.g. cm.

Within a note, typing @ offers the tags that apply: @field for an
				xsl:item-type; @param, @return and @error for a
				function or template; and @param, @variable, @author and
				@version for a module note. After @param, the parameter names without an
				@param yet are offered - and likewise after @field and @variable.
